{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Making a Difference", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Mother Teresa", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 14, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Understand actions, events, and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le14ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Past Continuous Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use the <span class=\"italic\">Past Continuous</span> or <span class=\"italic\">Past Progressive</span> tense to talk about an action that was  happening at a time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">How to form the Past Continuous:<br/> <span class=\"strong\">(was/were) + present participle (verb \u2013ing)</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the <span class=\"italic\">Past Continuous</span> when you are referring to actions that were in progress at a time in the past.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Remember that different subjects have different <span class=\"italic\">be</span> forms.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Negative form of the Past Continuous</span>:<br/> <span class=\"strong\">(was/were) + NOT + present participle (verb \u2013ing)</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the <span class=\"italic\">Past Continuous</span> to show that an action was happening when another action occurred. The action in the continuous tense started before the other action or point in time and may continue to happen after.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">was watching</span> TV at 10 pm last night.</span> (I started watching TV before 10 pm and was still watching at 10 pm.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Maria <span class=\"strong\">was cooking</span> dinner when her husband came home. </span>(Maria was in the middle of cooking dinner when her husband came home.)<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Maria cooked dinner when her husband came home.</span> (If you use Simple Past for both clauses, it means that her husband came home first and then Maria cooked dinner.)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you want to tell a story or relate events that happened, you can use the <span class=\"italic\">Past Continuous</span> to describe the scene or background. You will probably use a mix of the <span class=\"italic\">Simple Past</span> and the <span class=\"italic\">Past Continuous</span> since the <span class=\"italic\">Simple Past</span> describes the actions in the past.<br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">It was midnight. Anna was in bed but she couldn't sleep. The rain <span class=\"strong\">was falling</span> in sheets and the trees <span class=\"strong\">were blowing</span> in the strong winds. A branch <span class=\"strong\">was knocking</span> against the window of her bedroom. She was scared and wanted to call a friend to come over. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "She was still doing her religious training in 1928 when she went to India. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "As they were working, Mother Teresa and her Missionaries of Charity became known for helping the poor and the starving. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "However, she was still working every day until she could no longer.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Time Clause: Events at the Same Time", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use time clauses to link different clauses and events.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use time clauses to show that actions are happening at the same time (or simultaneous actions).  <br/> Time clauses are dependent clauses and must be connected to a main clause to form a complete sentence. It can come before or after a main clause. It is followed by a comma if it comes first.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the conjunctions <span class=\"strong\">as</span>, <span class=\"strong\">when</span> and <span class=\"strong\">while</span> for: <ul><li>actions that are in progress in the background when another action happens. You usually use continuous tenses with the longer actions. <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">Someone rang the doorbell <span class=\"strong\">as</span> I was cleaning the apartment. </span></i:><li><span class=\"italic\">Someone rang the doorbell <span class=\"strong\">when</span> I was cleaning the apartment. </span></i:><li><span class=\"italic\">Someone rang the doorbell <span class=\"strong\">while</span> I was cleaning the apartment</span>.</li></ul></i:></span>  <li>two longer situations happening at the same time. You use <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">while</span></span> more commonly with continuous verb forms. <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li><span class=\"strong\">While</span> I was taking a shower, my sister was brushing her teeth.</li></ul></i:></span>  <li>something that happened at a particular time in the past <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li><span class=\"strong\">When</span> I was in university, I joined the swim team.</li></ul></i:></span>  <li>you also use <span class=\"strong\">as</span> when you want to say that something changes at the same time as another event starts. <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li><span class=\"strong\">As</span> I was feeding my baby brother, I realized he had a fever.</li></ul></i:></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "She was still doing her religious training in 1928 <span class=\"strong\">when</span> she went to India. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">While</span> she was serving as the principal in a Catholic high school in Calcutta, Mother Teresa was moved by the number of sick people in the city's streets. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "However, she was still working every day <span class=\"strong\">until</span> she could no longer.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">As</span> they were working, Mother Teresa and her Missionaries of Charity became known for helping the poor and the starving. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "loss ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the fact or process of losing something or someone", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Her death was a great loss to many, but most of all, to the sick and the poor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le14ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "You use these words to talk about social issues.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "convent", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a \u200bbuilding or \u200bgroup of \u200bbuildings in which \u200bnuns (religious women) \u200blive or \u200bworship", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When she was 18 years old, she left her comfortable home and joined a convent in Ireland.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le14ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "vow", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a solemn promise ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There, she took her vows. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le14ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "starving", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a state of suffering from hunger", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Mother Teresa and her Missionaries of Charity became known for helping the poor and the starving. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le14ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "suffering", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the state of undergoing pain, distress, or hardship", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Officials gave Mother Teresa an old temple so she could open a home for the sick and suffering.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le14ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "orphanage", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a group  home for children without parents", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: One year later, Mother Teresa's first orphanage was opened, and in 1957, the Missionaries of Charity began working with people who had leprosy. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le14ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "leprosy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a contagious disease that affects the skin, mucous membranes, and nerves, causing discoloration and lumps", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: One year later, Mother Teresa's first orphanage was opened, and in 1957, the Missionaries of Charity began working with people who had leprosy. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le14ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "on behalf of ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something completed for someone else", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  In 1979 she was awarded a Nobel Peace Prize for her efforts on behalf of the sick and poor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le14ob05aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online or to the library and look up someone who does charity work. It could be an athlete or a film star.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find out what charity they support and how they support them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find out why they do this charitable work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a 200-word article on your person.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your article to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I find out about someone who does charity work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about what they support, how and why.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my article with another person.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn11le14ob05re2aud01", "images": [{"image": "engenn11le14ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "", "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn11le14ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "Mother Teresa of Calcutta was one of the most charitable women in history. Her death was a great loss to many, but most of all, to the sick and the poor.<br/>\nMother Teresa was born in 1910 in Albania. When she was 18 years old, she left her comfortable home and joined a convent in Ireland. There she chose her name, Sister Teresa, in memory of Saint Th\u00e9r\u00e8se of Lisieux.", "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn11le14ob05re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "She was still doing her religious training in 1928 when she went to India. There, she took her vows. While she was serving as the principal in a Catholic high school in Calcutta, Mother Teresa was moved by the number of sick people in the city's streets. People were living without hope. People were dying without comfort. In 1948, she left the convent to serve the sick. Two years later, she established a new order of sisters which she called the Missionaries of Charity.<br/> As they were working, Mother Teresa and her Missionaries of Charity became known for helping the poor and the starving. <br/> While she was working in Calcutta in 1952, officials gave Mother Teresa an old temple so she could open a home for the sick and suffering. She and the nuns were often seen gathering the dying from the streets of Calcutta and bringing them to a warm, clean environment. They were doing important work. They were making a difference.", "time": "25000"}, {"image": "engenn11le14ob05re2img03.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "One year later, Mother Teresa's first orphanage was opened, and in 1957, the Missionaries of Charity began working with people who had leprosy. These people were living away from others. They were not getting help, and her work was extending to hundreds of places around the world. In 1979, she was awarded a Nobel Peace Prize for her efforts on behalf of the sick and poor.<br/> In 1990, Mother Teresa was slowing down.  Her health was failing. However, she was still working every day until she could no longer. Her work and good deeds will be remembered for years to come.", "time": "87000"}], "coverimg": "engenn11le14ob05re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "img_path": "", "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about social issues, beliefs and opinions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about what was happening.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about events in the past that took place at the same time.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What do you know about Mother Teresa?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What organizations do charitable work in your city?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " When might you consider doing some work for one?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": " Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": " Charity work is fulfilling!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": []}, {"id": 1, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " \nMother Teresa  started <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">Missionaries</span> of Charity.\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Click on the play button to listen to the audio.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": [{"content": "A <span class=\"italic\">\u201cmissionary\u201d</span> is part of a religious group and works in service to help others.", "type": "text", "tip_id": 0}], "type": "tips"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}]}], "type": "STI", "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0, "responses": [{"correct": 0, "id": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "id": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected"